t  tech and combat abilities they have  famous parents who are no longer around  and were both betrayed by their mentor  evil groups are a big problem for these  characters  as batman has ties with the league of  shadows and iron man with the 10 rings  luckily they each have a trusty  assistant to help them out  i don't deserve you often no sir you  don't  captain america and wonder woman are the  star-spangled heroes that represent the  good in humanity  they both don costumes with red and blue  color schemes  and of course they both wield shields  they each fought in a world war and had  a ragtag team of soldiers with them as  backup  even more both these characters lost  their loves during the war  and in each case a sacrifice involving a  plane was the cause  these are extremely smart and  sharp-witted characters who are the  voice of reason for their superhero  groups  every time someone tries to win a war  before it starts innocent people die  raya and the last dragon is a welcome  addition to the disney family  proving that mulan isn't the only one  that can kick butt with the sword  their fierceness and selflessness make  these two of the strongest disney  characters  what they do they do for others namely  their fathers  mulan steps up to take her father's  place in the military while raya goes on  a journey to bring her father back to  life  the strong bonds they have with their  fathers is what drives them forward  and they don't let any obstacles get in  their way also  we have to mention that they both have a  fun dragon as a sidekick  drag gun not lizard i don't do that  tongue thing  a disney princess can't ask for a better  wingman than lumiere or sebastian  these two are the fun lovable right hand  man to their princess  supporting them through and through  finding love isn't easy  but these two make sure the princess  meets her prince whether through a  lovely song  or the perfect mood lighting and of  course who can forget the incredibly  catchy tunes  be our guest and under the sea these two  never fail  to make the moment  don't we all wish we had a gandalf or  obi-wan in our lives  a wise old mentor donning a robe and  yielding a sword who's connected with a  magical force  that can help us along in our journey to  restore balance to the world  yeah that would be awesome especially  given that these two mentors were  willing to sacrifice themselves to help  the hero  these are definitely the best mentors  one can ask for  just don't betray them like their  friends did you were my brother  the two speedsters of marvel and dc  respectively  flash and quicksilver will always be  mentioned together when it comes to  superheroes with super speed  they are both loners who don't have much  outside of family  until they're recruited by a team and  they're incredibly witty  always injecting a well-needed dose of  humor to whatever scene they're in  these speedsters just keep going and  going  i need friends shrek and carl  fredrickson  surprisingly yes when you look at their  personalities and stories  they're actually very similar they're  grumpy lonely men who just want to be  left alone  but people keep invading their land they  have a funny sidekick friend who is  forced upon them  and drags them on an adventure and while  they find this friend  annoying at first they come to enjoy  their company by the end of the story  learning to love others the only  question we have is what would it be  like if these characters ever met each  other  this is my swamp the clown prince of  crime and the split personality of  norman osborne are two of the most  menacing villains in comics they are  crazy  unstable and just all around psychotic  you can never predict what they may do  as they always keep our heroes on their  toes they get their joy from torturing  and taunting the protagonists  their family and friends whether it's  mary jane or rachel dawes  no one is safe from these two and  they're creepy smiling  with new 